__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
data/receipts/post-commit-*.json
data/wiki-update/
.serena/
.openwiki-review/
proof_workflow/data/
# A -dirty proof stamp binds bytes that were never present at its named commit.
# Keep settled proof/control receipts reviewable; discard only this noisy class.
data/proof-workflow/*-dirty.json
.grepai/
data/ingest/
# One directory per notebooklm harvest. Evidence of a run, and the extracted
# text belongs to somebody else's Google documents — the receipt beside it
# carries the sha256, which is what pins a claim to a run without publishing it.
data/notebooklm/
# What a sandboxed codex turn wrote, one directory per run. Evidence of a run,
# not part of the repo: committing it would put an agent's draft on main before
# anyone read it.
data/codex-sandbox/
# Paired auto-permission measurements, one directory per experiment. Evidence,
# not source: the numbers belong in whatever writes them up, not on main.
data/automode-bench/
.container-home/
# Native worktrees live here. Each one is a git repository, so a `git add -A`
# stages it as an embedded repo — a clone of this repo would carry a pointer to
# something it cannot fetch, and the fast-quality gate FATALs on a path it
# cannot read. Caught exactly that way. This is the shape fix: the guard belongs
# where every caller already routes, not in each person remembering.
.claude/worktrees/
